   "etymology": "From Proto-Albanian *e(k)šta, ultimately from Proto-Indo-European *h₁eǵʰs-tos (compare Ancient Greek ἐκτός (ektós, “outside”)), suffixed form of *h₁eǵʰs, whence Latin ex (compare also extra, exter from *h₁eǵʰs-tro-, *h₁eǵʰs-ter), Ancient Greek ἐξ (ex), Old Church Slavonic из (iz). Compare the now obsolete Albanian ith, probably from *h₁eǵʰs, and ish derived from a variant form *eḱs.",
   "etymology_class": "inherited",
   "source_lang": null,
